Falsifies `address_space_map::verification::pair_page_accepts_every_page_of_its_band`.

The defect: an off-by-one in `pair_page`'s band check, which asks about the page after `va`, so
the last page of `PAIR_PAGES` is refused.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that no allowed address reaches `pair_page`'s asserts; Kani
reports "a pair page must lie in PAIR_PAGES" reachable at `va = 0x0FFF_F000`.

diff --git a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
index 0eba0def7..9e7ef0e0e 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@ pub const CURRENT_CPU_PAGE: u64 = PROCESS_PAGES.end - PAGE;
 pub const fn pair_page(va: u64) -> u64 {
     assert!(va.is_multiple_of(PAGE), "a pair page must be page aligned");
     assert!(
-        PAIR_PAGES.contains(va),
+        PAIR_PAGES.contains(va + PAGE),
         "a pair page must lie in PAIR_PAGES (address_space_map)"
     );
     va
